			"notes": "- Supports Minecraft 26.3.\n\n0.3.0 never reached Modrinth, so its changes ship here too:\n\n- Mob previews are the real entity model now, rendered by the game itself, so modded mobs work and small mobs are framed sensibly.\n- Markers are sized by true perspective, exactly like a name tag, with a floor so a distant ping stays readable.\n- Previews no longer jitter as you move.\n- Own colour palette. A player's colour also recolours their dot on the locator bar, and any player can override it.\n- The ping sound is directional, and which sound it is can now be picked from a list of vanilla ones.\n- Rebindable keys for pinging, pinging a block and opening the settings.\n- New Preview target setting: previews when sneaking, when not sneaking, or never."
		}
